    "position_note": "The footprint's south-west corner (local E 475.11, N -348.02): the building is centred in the square as both pictures show it, the square being the block the 1871 plan's LaSalle, Clark, Randolph and Washington Streets enclose (lot lines E 474.4-566.0, N -384.3 to -273.0), squared to Washington Street (89.53 degrees). Good to the plan's tracing of Mitchell's map, a few metres. IT LAPS THE 1835 PLAT'S CLARK STREET BY 4.06 m, AND THAT IS REFUSED IN WRITING, NOT REPAIRED (T-3688; tools/corridor_intrusion_baseline.json `refused`). The corridor is derived from the 1835 street control; the square is the 1871 plan's, traced from Mitchell's 1870 map, which is what the 1871 scene draws. The two tracings disagree by about 4 m here, and moving the building 4.1 m west to clear the older one would take it off the centre of the square both pictures show it on.",
