  "research_note": "THE COURT HOUSE, built by T-3688 for the 1871 scene. From Lovejoy & Foster's stereograph of 1871 from Clark and Randolph Streets and Andreas's engraving 'The Court-House before the fire' (vol. 2, p. 65) from Clark and Washington: the 1853 house of Lockport marble in the middle under its domed cupola with the fire watch's balcony and the clock, a smaller octagonal belfry and domed cupola on its roof, and the two Lemont-stone wings of 1870 east and west, each with a scrolled crest over its centre pavilion and low domes on its corners. The plan sizes are the 1853 house's (Andreas vol. 1, p. 181) and the wings read off the two pictures (docs/LIBERTIES.md, T-3688).",
